 ## Background
-The concept of Neural Radiance Fields was introduced by Mildenhall et al. in 2020 [S1]. The method implicitly represents a radiance field using an MLP, computing pixel color by accumulating samples along camera rays via volume rendering [S1]. The MLP takes a point $p$ as input and outputs density $\sigma$ and color $c$ [S1]. The training objective minimizes the reconstruction loss between the reconstructed color and ground-truth color $C_{gt}(\mathbf{r})$ [S1].
+The concept of Neural Radiance Fields was introduced by Mildenhall et al. in 2020 [S1]. The method implicitly represents a radiance field using an MLP, computing pixel color by accumulating samples along camera rays via volume rendering [S1]. The MLP takes a 3D point $p$ as input and outputs its density $\sigma$ and color $\mathbf{c}$ [S1]. The network is trained with a reconstruction loss between the reconstructed color and ground-truth color $C_{gt}(\mathbf{r})$, defined as $\mathcal{L}_{rec} = \sum_{\mathbf{r} \in \mathcal{R}} \| \hat{C}(\mathbf{r}) - C_{gt}(\mathbf{r}) \|_2^2$ [S1].
 
